World Health Organization. *WHO good manufacturing practices for sterile pharmaceutical products*, Technical Report Series 1044, Annex 2, 2022, printed pages 87–169. [Official annex](https://www.who.int/publications/m/item/trs1044-annex2) · [Complete 83-page PDF](https://cdn.who.int/media/docs/default-source/medicines/norms-and-standards/guidelines/production/trs1044-annex-2-gmp-for-sterile-pharmaceutical-products.pdf).

Read the full annex progressively: principles and quality systems, premises, equipment, utilities, personnel, production, environmental/process monitoring and quality control. Follow how design and continuing control support evidence; a finished-product test alone cannot establish all that happened during production.

Title, contents and selected principles were inspected on 30 October 2026. The [WHO catalogue for the complete fifty-sixth report](https://www.who.int/publications/b/66472) identifies CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 IGO; preserve its attribution, component exceptions and adaptation conditions. This is the identified 2022 guidance, not a declaration of present legal obligations in every jurisdiction. Technical procedures require their application-specific context. All documents remain external.

